   "confidence": "1.00",
   "confidence_pct": 100,
   "reasoning": "TSMC signalled an acceleration in AI-related demand through a significant upward revision of its full-year 2026 capital budget and the identification of a new growth driver. In the Q4 2025 call (15 January 2026), the company guided a 2026 capital budget of \"USD52 billion and USD56 billion\". By the Q2 2026 call (16 July 2026), management explicitly stated they had \"decided to raise our full-year 2026 capital budget to be between USD60 billion and USD64 billion\". This increase was specifically attributed to \"continued strong structural demand from our customers, including the newly emerging agentic AI market\". Because TSMC explicitly links its capital expenditures to \"growth opportunities in following years,\" increasing the budget specifically to support \"newly emerging\" AI demand constitutes a signal that growth is accelerating relative to the previous outlook.",
